# Schafbergbahn: the steam cog train (moving platform, D-067). A historic
# rack loco on the LEFT (downhill end) pushes one coach uphill, as on the
# real line. Loco: black boiler k/d with m top light and i bands, a flared
# spark-arrester funnel (the only thing above the roof, rows 0-7, x 0-5),
# steam dome, pine-green cab G/j with the driver, red frame and wheels R with
# o crank pins, an i coupling rod and a d/m cog wheel between the axles.
# Coach: wine R wooden body, o window frames and band (cream `c` would be a
# fill, art-style 8), b/s windows full of B passengers, l panel joints.
# The bodies are built level (the hitbox is a horizontal 64x32 box); only the
# undercarriage follows the 1:4 incline.
#
# Walking surface: row 8 (k edge, i lip at row 9, m at 10) across all 64 px.
#
# Track contract for the renderer (sprite-local, origin 32,40): the top
# rail's pixel row under sprite column x is 41 - floor(x / 4); the wheels
# stand on it (wheel bottom = that row - 1). In world space with the body's
# left edge at L and its bottom at B (= origin y): rail row(X) =
# B + 1 - floor((X - L) / 4), fixed to the spawn position. Drawn per column
# with u = X - L (behind the train): row Y `d` upper rail, Y+1 `m` rack
# teeth on even u (odd u transparent), Y+2 `m` rack bar, Y+3 `d` lower rail;
# sleeper columns (u mod 8 in {0,1}) `O` over Y+1..Y+4; a `d` girder line
# at Y+5 under the whole track. The top rail stays `d` (no light lip).
# See the M4 catalog as-built note.
# Built with a throwaway generator script, frozen here; the grids are the
# source.
sprite = schafbergbahn
size   = 64x40
origin = 32,40
hitbox = 0,8,64,32
anim   = idle frames=1
anim   = ride frames=2 ticks=8 loop
---
